Step-by-Step Development Questions for Full Banking Application
This document contains a complete set of step-by-step development questions to guide the implementation of the Full Banking Application project using C# and Object-Oriented Programming concepts.
1. Project Planning & Requirement Analysis
1. What is the main purpose of the banking application?
2. Who are the target users of the system (Admin, Staff, Customer)?
3. What are the functional requirements of the system?
4. What are the non-functional requirements of the system?
5. What banking operations should the system support?
6. How will data be stored in the system?
7. What security features are required for the application?
8. What technologies and tools will be used?
2. System Design Questions
1. What classes are required for the system?
2. What attributes should be included in the Account class?
3. What methods should be included in the Account class?
4. How should inheritance be implemented between SavingAccount and CurrentAccount?
5. What properties should the User class contain?
6. How will interfaces be used in the project?
7. How should transaction history be managed?
8. How should account numbers be generated uniquely?
3. Login & Authentication
1. How will users log in to the system?
2. How should admin and staff roles be differentiated?
3. How should invalid login attempts be handled?
4. How will default admin accounts be created?
5. How should passwords be stored securely?
6. How will session management work?
4. Account Creation Module
1. What information is required to create a bank account?
2. How will the system validate user input?
3. How will account types be selected?
4. How will account numbers be generated?
5. How will duplicate accounts be prevented?
6. What initial balance rules should be implemented?
7. How will account details be saved into JSON files?
5. Deposit Module
1. How will users select an account for deposit?
2. How will deposit amounts be validated?
3. What happens after a successful deposit?
4. How will transaction history be updated after deposits?
5. How will invalid deposit attempts be handled?
6. Withdrawal Module
1. How will users withdraw money from an account?
2. How will insufficient balance conditions be checked?
3. What withdrawal limits should be implemented?
4. How will failed withdrawals be handled?
5. How will transaction history record withdrawals?
7. Transfer Module
1. How will money transfers between accounts work?
2. How will sender and receiver accounts be validated?
3. How will transfer amounts be checked?
4. How will transaction history record transfers?
5. How will failed transfers be handled?
8. Account Viewing & Balance Checking
1. How will all accounts be displayed?
2. How will account searching work?
3. How will balance inquiries be handled?
4. How should account information be formatted on screen?
9. Transaction History
1. How will transaction history be stored?
2. What details should each transaction contain?
3. How will transaction history be displayed?
4. How will transaction records be filtered?
10. File Handling & Data Storage
1. How will JSON serialization work in the project?
2. How will user data be loaded from files?
3. How will account data be saved into files?
4. How will missing files be handled?
5. How will corrupted data files be handled?
11. Validation & Error Handling
1. How will null or empty inputs be validated?
2. How will invalid account numbers be handled?
3. How will invalid numeric values be prevented?
4. How will exceptions be managed in the system?
5. How will user-friendly error messages be displayed?
12. Object-Oriented Programming Concepts
1. How is encapsulation implemented in the system?
2. How is inheritance used in the banking application?
3. How is polymorphism implemented?
4. How are interfaces used?
5. Why is abstraction important in this project?
13. Testing Questions
1. How will unit testing be performed?
2. How will login functionality be tested?
3. How will deposit and withdrawal operations be tested?
4. How will transfer functionality be tested?
5. How will file handling be tested?
6. How will edge cases be tested?
14. UI & User Experience
1. How should the console menu be designed?
2. How will users navigate through the system?
3. How should success and error messages be displayed?
4. How will the system improve user experience?
15. Security & Future Improvements
1. How can the application be secured further?
2. How can password encryption be implemented?
3. How can database integration be added in the future?
4. How can a graphical user interface (GUI) be implemented?
5. How can online banking features be added?
6. How can mobile banking integration be implemented?
16. Viva & Presentation Preparation
1. Why did you choose C# for this project?
2. Why did you use JSON files instead of a database?
3. What challenges did you face during development?
4. How did you solve those challenges?
5. What are the main features of the system?
6. How does the account creation process work?
7. How is OOP applied in the project?
8. What improvements can be added in future versions?
